//? Title: A VAE with a Conditional Affine-Flow Posterior
//? Subtitle: Explicit change of variables, live image context and a sample-only decoder
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An invertible transformation can turn a diagonal-Gaussian approximate posterior into a more
flexible distribution. This report derives two alternating affine couplings, checks their full
Jacobian and analytic inverse, and trains a compact784-pixel VAE on294 unique known-factor
images. The image encoder conditions the posterior flow; only its final four-coordinate sample
reaches the Bernoulli decoder. Twenty-one visible Adam updates and fixed four-draw validation
select epoch3. Heldout NLL226.570 plus sampled log-density ratio36.836 gives negative ELBO263.405
nats/image. Decode(f(mu)) MSE0.06882 is worse than the fitting-only mean0.04855. Unfiltered
reconstructions and all20 prior codes retain that failure. Posterior flexibility alone proves
neither better inference than a matched baseline nor useful semantic generation.
)
\toc

> Change the inference family, keep the generative model

[Rezende and Mohamed's Variational Inference with Normalizing Flows](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v37/rezende15.html)
constructs flexible approximate posteriors by transforming simpler base samples. Here the base
encoder is784→32ReLU→two linear four-coordinate Gaussian heads. Supply epsilon~N(0,I),
then z0=mu(x)+exp(l(x)/2)⊙epsilon. Two2+2 affine couplings produce z1 and final z2.
Each coupling receives the same **live**32-coordinate image context. This amortizes its
parameters without feeding the context directly into the decoder.

The generative model remains p(z2)=N(0,I) and p(x|z2), a4→32ReLU→784-logit Bernoulli
decoder. Prior samples are final codes z2~N(0,I), decoded directly. Passing them through an
image-conditioned posterior flow would define a different generative model. This is neither
an image-space exact-likelihood flow nor a learned flow prior.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/flow_vae_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram          d(52, 1200);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle wide;
  wide.width  = 4.6;
  wide.height = 2.6;
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke dash;
  dash.arrow  = true;
  dash.dashed = true;
