> Measured results and weak controls

Epoch3 is selected: heldout NLL226.569573, sampled logq−logp36.835837 and negative
ELBO263.405410 nats/image. Mean forward logdet1.032068 is a density correction,
not KL or a reconstruction score. Signed sample ratios remain in the saved outputs.
Decode(f(mu)) MSE0.068817722 is worse than fitting mean0.048548290. For nonlinear flows,
f(mu) is not generally E_q[z]; its decode is not the posterior predictive mean. This
single-seed, short run has no matched no-flow ablation, so it does not establish a tighter
bound or better inference. Negative ELBO is not exact marginal log likelihood.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/flow_vae_learning.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream f("build/flow_vae/history.tsv");
  std::string   line;
  std::getline(f, line);
  std::vector<double> epoch, nll, elbo;
  while (std::getline(f, line)) {
    std::istringstream r(line);
    double             e, train, a, ratio, det, total;
    r >> e >> train >> a >> ratio >> det >> total;
    epoch.push_back(e);
    nll.push_back(a);
    elbo.push_back(total);
  }
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  chart.lines(epoch, nll, "validation NLL", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .lines(epoch, elbo, "validation negative ELBO", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .title("Fixed four-draw validation / completed epochs")
      .x_label("completed epoch")
      .y_label("nats per image")
      .save_svg("build/flow_vae_learning.svg");
}
