> Reproduction evidence and binding scope

The report preserves the source's19 NPZ archives by dtype, shape and every value byte,
including all18 fields at zero noise and four draws for every pool, first gradients/update,
all epochs, selected arrays, Gaussian banks and the48-entry coupling Jacobian. Batch/source
orders and complete validation histories are compared exactly. A separate optional NumPy
oracle checks all52,672 first derivatives, the first Float32 Adam step, all posterior/inverse/
prior predictions, explicit noise, density corrections and all three eligible criteria.
It performs no fitting, downloads or data preparation.

```
python3 scripts/check_flow_variational_autoencoder.py docs/mepml/examples/nn/2_autoencoders/2.2_variational_autoencoders/build/flow_vae --json build/nn-report-conversion/flow_vae/oracle.json
```

Reusable native APIs are ConditionalAffinePosteriorFlow and FlowVariationalAutoencoder;
GaussianVaeDecode provides final-code-only inference. C++ outputs and all18 named archive
handles own lifetime. Python and R expose the same operations; tests retain fields across
collection, exercise explicit host Adam, verify live context derivatives, both coupling
directions and target-free decoding. This API addition does not mark incomplete independent
Python/R experiment loops as native ports. Full Jacobian and finite-difference checks include
context/conditioner paths rather than assuming a diagonal Jacobian. No semantic generation,
rate-distortion or benchmark-quality claim follows from this tiny run.
